@startuml deployment-background-jobs-dev
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: background jobs on dev need one new pod (ocr) and no new transport: every
'       Celery worker, the catalog's own and each service's, publishes its task
'       events to Redis db 7, where the catalog's event listener (pod
'       evilflowers-beat) writes the one job ledger in postgresql18; services report
'       results to one catalog endpoint, and the portal reads and controls jobs
'       only through the catalog API.
' Kind: UML deployment diagram, instance level, proposal (IP-031). Artifacts listed
'       as text inside the nodes. Scope: job dispatch, events, reports and control.
'       Omitted: readium, flower, maildev, tei-*, the VPN, telemetry (every pod
'       sends OTLP to its node's alloy-node as today), prod (Compose on gateway:
'       one evilflowers container runs gunicorn, worker, beat and the listener
'       under supervisord; no OCR worker until a deployment decision).
' Source: Mimir kube_pod_info{namespace="evilflowers-dev"} (2026-11-14 19:39 UTC);
'         knowledge ansible/roles/evilflowers_k8s/templates/evilflowers.yaml.j2
'         (catalog_split: evilflowers, evilflowers-worker, evilflowers-beat with
'         containers beat + events); conf/supervisor.conf;
'         apps/tasks/management/commands/celery_event_handler.py;
'         evilflowers_catalog/settings/base.py CELERY_*; evilflowers-ocr-worker
'         ef4311d; diagrams deployment-k8s-dev-environment and
'         deployment-lcp-encryption-dev (2026-11-08); EvilFlowersCatalog#146.
' =============================================================================

title Background jobs on dev: one ledger, one listener, one report endpoint (proposal, 2026-11-14)

node portal <<device>> [
**Admin browser**
----
elvira-portal · Background jobs
]

node "**gateway** · 192.168.122.227" <<virtualMachine>> as gw {
  node edge <<webServer>> [
**nginx** (host) → **cilium-envoy** :8082
----
dev → HTTPRoute evilflowers
]
  node bridge <<container>> [
**k8s-bridge** · nginx stream
:5432 · :6379
]
  node "**Docker Engine** · network elvira" <<executionEnvironment>> as docker {
    node redis <<container>> [
**redis** 172.28.1.2 · db 7
----
task lists: celery,
evilflowers_ocr_worker, …
events: celeryev fanout
control: celery.pidbox
]
    node pg <<container>> [
**postgresql18** 172.28.1.1
----
jobs (spec · desired · state)
job_protocols (runs) · job_events
]
  }
}

node "**control** · 192.168.122.60 · k3s" <<virtualMachine>> as ct {
  frame "**evilflowers-dev** · namespace" as nsdev {
    node web <<container>> [
**evilflowers** · gunicorn :8000
----
/api/v1/jobs (apply · patch ·
list · runs report)
JobFacade · reconcile
]
    node workers <<container>> [
**Celery workers** ×6 deployments
----
**evilflowers-worker** (catalog)
**lcpencrypt** · **analyzer** · **image**
**equation** · **text** ×3
]
    node beat <<container>> <<focus>> [
**evilflowers-beat**
----
container beat: schedules,
reconcile · sweep · prune
container events:
celery_event_handler (ledger)
]
    node ocr <<container>> <<proposed>> [
**ocr** · Celery worker -E
evilflowers-ocr-service
----
queue evilflowers_ocr_worker
ocrmypdf skip_text
]
    artifact pvc <<volume>> [
**evilflowers-dev/data** · PVC
----
catalogs/…/{acquisition}.pdf
catalogs/…/ocr/{job}.pdf (new)
]
  }
}

' ---- layout only ------------------------------------------------------------------
' gateway above control: one leaf of each linked (diagram guide).
redis -[hidden]right- pg
redis -[hidden]down- web
web -[hidden]right- beat
beat -[hidden]right- workers
web -[hidden]down- ocr

' ---- reading and controlling jobs -----------------------------------------------
portal --> edge : HTTPS :443
edge --> web : HTTP :8000\n/api/v1/jobs

' ---- everything meets in Redis db 7 and postgresql18, through the bridge ----------
' Each pod's Redis and SQL connections are one edge; the bridge forwards both.
bridge <-- web : Redis db 7 LPUSH · revoke\nSQL :5432
bridge <-[$accent()]- beat : <b>Redis db 7 SUBSCRIBE celeryev</b>\n<b>SQL :5432 job ledger</b>
bridge <-- workers : Redis db 7\nconsume · events
bridge <-[$accent()]- ocr : <b>Redis db 7</b>\n<b>consume · events</b>
bridge --> redis : TCP :6379
bridge --> pg : TCP :5432

' ---- results come back over HTTP --------------------------------------------------
web <-- ocr : HTTP :8000 POST\njobs/runs/{run}/report
web <-- workers : HTTP :8000\nexisting hooks

ocr ..> pvc : <<mount>>

$legend_live_proposed()

caption The only new workload is the ocr pod; it uses the paths lcpencrypt and the extraction workers already use.\nEvery worker sends task events (-E; the catalog's own through CELERY_WORKER_SEND_TASK_EVENTS),\nso the listener in evilflowers-beat sees every task of every worker and records it as a run of its job.\nThe portal never talks to Redis or a worker: it declares jobs at /api/v1/jobs (apply, patch);\nthe reconciler sends runs, and revokes a cancelled job's run (pidbox, same Redis).
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/deployment-background-jobs-dev.puml
